/S /P
/P 3827 0 R
/E (If there are multiple red/green objects detected, it only feeds the largest and closest \(low y-coordinate\) one to the main code. This prevents the robot from trying to go in 2 directions at once)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3828 0 R
/E (The pink colour has priority over everything else, so the first step \(except in parking\) is to move away from the pink centroid)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 347 0 R
/E (Why HSV over ML?)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3829 0 R
/E (We have chosen to use an HSV pipeline over AI/Machine Learning models as it has a much higher frame rate and a lower latency)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3830 0 R
/E (In addition, HSV can be calibrated extremely fast, while ML requires a huge database of photos. Taking all these photos in the lighting at a competition would consume a lot of time)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
